#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078136 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "31a9b20e-d159-5ff2-94dc-54b8d7b8e620" :question/math-academy-id "e-21785" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3,$ then calculate $D(e^{3x}).$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} +  f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = y,  f_2 = 0,  f_1 = -1,$ and $f_0 = y^2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y = e^{3x}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{3x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{3x})+{({e}^{3x})}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & =27{e}^{6x}-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}({e}^{6x}+27{e}^{3x}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078256 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "91e7f8e9-dc03-5203-9d33-0175960ba276" :question/math-academy-id "e-6570" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{- x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  $a_2 = 1, a_1 = 3,$ and $a_0 = 5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+5){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{-x})+3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078257 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/id #uuid "0fba12b1-fa78-5ff2-88e4-2a690105d321" :question/math-academy-id "e-6571" :question/problem "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9,$ and $f_0 = 0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-5x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-5x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00d1af61-7a8f-560b-b405-edfcffdf54a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{-2x}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297532} {:answer/id #uuid "68f2ca65-5a4f-5381-9784-5f59754c4ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297533} {:answer/id #uuid "ca16b756-5df7-5ab3-a11b-62a5aa2dfcaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297534} {:answer/id #uuid "c201d735-0a4f-5f1c-93c8-f786e8f3e023" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2x}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297535} {:answer/id #uuid "b5203320-3320-59bc-8139-c24e2e0e0751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68f2ca65-5a4f-5381-9784-5f59754c4ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297533} :answer-field/id #uuid "72f22110-bf8b-551c-8ff9-5ada3c1421f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "609ba886-ad8b-5aa8-9b0a-02bc64695179" :question/math-academy-id "q-130083" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={e}^{-2x}+x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=2,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-2x}+x) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})({e}^{-2x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-2x}+x)+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-2x}+x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{e}^{-2x}+1)+2(-2{e}^{-2x}+1) \\\\  & =4{e}^{-2x}-4{e}^{-2x}+2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a4a8ac2-d585-548a-b9d0-f4d080662ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{4x}(2 - x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075928} {:answer/id #uuid "8d77a835-088d-52d9-9e43-db86fb3b03df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{4x}(3 - x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075929} {:answer/id #uuid "cbc33d01-4b42-572c-aafd-dbd2deb86df9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{4x}(2 + x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075930} {:answer/id #uuid "6985173e-1544-57f9-8947-41f91def3dc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{4x}(1 + 3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075931} {:answer/id #uuid "7ffb8862-d0a4-5249-9c91-1d37b54e476a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{4x}(3 + x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d77a835-088d-52d9-9e43-db86fb3b03df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e^{4x}(3 - x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075929} :answer-field/id #uuid "53fc149f-aae5-5029-89df-43db5112179f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3aca8975-6bdc-5d74-9fd7-116773d083f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-337559" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2},$ then $D({e}^{2x})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=2y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={e}^{2x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{2x}) & ={e}^{2x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{2x})-x({e}^{2x})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{2x})+2({e}^{2x})^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{2x})-x{e}^{2x}\\cdot 2{e}^{2x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 4{e}^{2x}-2x{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}-2x{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =6{e}^{4x}-2x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =2{e}^{4x}(3-x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5dd7583-7f36-546f-bc64-1f944e9f2905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297539} {:answer/id #uuid "e1a4f880-51c1-57f4-b32e-0af488492101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297540} {:answer/id #uuid "4f7a37a7-e31c-50b4-aac1-e2f253eade87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297541} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1eaf7e-2e18-52c6-b027-8cf0e95a021b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297542} {:answer/id #uuid "86b2dcc3-fee0-5913-b48d-b54ad9350a7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d5dd7583-7f36-546f-bc64-1f944e9f2905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{e}^{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297539} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcef8dbd-13a7-51ea-b786-ab14b62d89aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47ba9895-f02e-5f8b-92fd-e876a7c7f3e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-337830" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-2,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={e}^{2x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=3,$ and ${a}_{0}=-2.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{2x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-2){e}^{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{2x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{2x})-2\\cdot {e}^{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{2x})+3\\cdot (2{e}^{2x})-2{e}^{2x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{2x}+6{e}^{2x}-2{e}^{2x} \\\\  & =8{e}^{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d6f7a39-32da-5684-ab63-42651a0b5717" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}+9{x}^{2}+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297546} {:answer/id #uuid "8563bc4b-2ab8-5fc1-8162-fdb0f1bf1666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x-9{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297547} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1a547d-aa5c-5b41-b636-0ba239e82476" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297548} {:answer/id #uuid "91d39ed7-6c0e-55f7-a851-414d323affca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297549} {:answer/id #uuid "017c802e-3cd3-5b1a-8aa1-b9d338250c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}-6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297550}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91d39ed7-6c0e-55f7-a851-414d323affca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297549} :answer-field/id #uuid "4054844e-d875-5394-9109-c9938be5f883" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56348ca5-95a9-5367-bd7f-5d20654a2a14" :question/math-academy-id "q-337835" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={x}^{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{2}=1,{a}_{1}=-3,$ and ${a}_{0}=4.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({x}^{3}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4){x}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{3})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+4\\cdot {x}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2})-3\\cdot (3{x}^{2})+4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =6x-9{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3} \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}-9{x}^{2}+6x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297551 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc09c034-6527-5638-a075-cde3368e77c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297553} {:answer/id #uuid "73178055-870e-502e-888d-e2f13ab0fdde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297554} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a5e378-8f3e-59db-b873-a2286eb0901a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297555} {:answer/id #uuid "50ae2fbe-eb3e-5e98-a101-37d4e25a01a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297556} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9132b9-dea5-5c6f-b163-6817fa33980c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50ae2fbe-eb3e-5e98-a101-37d4e25a01a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297556} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2533ffd-a752-5f4c-8c5e-efda36b89540" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297552}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e7cce31-e437-5488-a28b-54343e727c5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-337837" :question/problem "Given that $D=2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-2,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=2x,{f}_{1}=3,$ and ${f}_{0}=-2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =(2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+\\frac{3}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =2x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{3}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{3}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b39f5e-f9fc-57ae-8282-27d5ad3dc10d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297560} {:answer/id #uuid "079a0fa3-a3f9-5751-bf95-f203bc4fb9ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297561} {:answer/id #uuid "4723a33d-f6b6-5474-b89f-b0460010e71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297562} {:answer/id #uuid "a7814b1a-7112-5068-b556-d7e043539b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297563} {:answer/id #uuid "df9836fc-fe46-585c-a283-fc026f7d1c6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7814b1a-7112-5068-b556-d7e043539b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297563} :answer-field/id #uuid "e145c1b5-0cad-5893-9b05-732087ad8dec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae2d10ba-6bbb-5ff9-ab97-ca3ddf449ad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-337845" :question/problem "Given that $D=2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=2x,{f}_{1}=3,$ and ${f}_{0}=4.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =(2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4)\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}})+3(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}})+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{3}{4{x}^{5/2}}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5db4e0c-8ac3-50a9-b223-6c4bc4ae57fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297567} {:answer/id #uuid "e197b1f1-6a27-58bb-bf85-f351f1623bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2-2{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297568} {:answer/id #uuid "06c8ac3d-ef08-52cd-98a6-a7e8dd73c82c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297569} {:answer/id #uuid "af46432a-3c50-5a4b-8e49-8037b8d5b9e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297570} {:answer/id #uuid "8883c823-ac06-5254-8dc2-fbabda31a87f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2+{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5db4e0c-8ac3-50a9-b223-6c4bc4ae57fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297567} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a2a7949-f7a7-5b03-85b0-65d7cffb972b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42241a9b-a6a8-5c40-bd12-92c20975f581" :question/math-academy-id "q-337846" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{y}^{2},$ then $D({x}^{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=-2xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=3y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2})-2x({x}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+3({x}^{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)-2x({x}^{2})\\cdot 2x+3{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 2-4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{4} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838d80f6-f90d-56de-b5b6-b26e8e1ea828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}(3x^{2} + 6x^{2} + 2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075934} {:answer/id #uuid "bd70d18d-23a4-56f4-ab09-304c42c2e82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}(3x^{2} + 6x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075935} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e14521-174d-5bc6-ae30-62bda66ffaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}(3x^{2} - 6x - 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075936} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a409b9-c806-5961-9d6b-62affa9d4cce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}(3x^{2} - 6x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075937} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb0c6bd-643b-5013-a18c-08c28ea8ccf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}(3x^{2} - 6x^{2} + 2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd70d18d-23a4-56f4-ab09-304c42c2e82e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3}(3x^{2} + 6x + 2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075935} :answer-field/id #uuid "83db50a1-9e8c-5ed3-b7a8-e497a53bf91b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fb8f945-ebea-5867-aab8-11f8c05f5841" :question/math-academy-id "q-337986" :question/problem "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y,$ then $D({x}^{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=y,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{3}) & =x({x}^{3})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{3})+{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{x}^{2})+{x}^{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\cdot 6+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{4}+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+6x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99516970-e3aa-53f5-aab4-586fd11535b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin x(2 - (x - 1)\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075940} {:answer/id #uuid "a167f29f-e6e8-5d8b-965a-81fd5f801893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin x(2 + (x + 1)\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075941} {:answer/id #uuid "a4f1e5b0-c283-5332-9ded-6922685d8b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin x(2 - (x + 1)\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075942} {:answer/id #uuid "cf52e417-da39-5837-a653-fc17bdf3cae6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075943} {:answer/id #uuid "67f587fc-f0ad-5fca-b4a0-4969ab14600d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin x(-2 + (x + 1)\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4f1e5b0-c283-5332-9ded-6922685d8b45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin x(2 - (x + 1)\\cos x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075942} :answer-field/id #uuid "f169ba3b-207f-53b7-b871-36f49647115c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186075939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d6980d3-3dab-5809-bc7b-16920f6471c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-338253" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=y,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(2-(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Multivariable Functions as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5936ad5d-47c1-54c8-b496-760a09fa8130" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(6-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297574} {:answer/id #uuid "c93b093d-82c3-5b47-8a9a-c34b0321dc69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3+8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297575} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8641b5-6ade-5521-b3db-ca0bab88c272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297576} {:answer/id #uuid "a238c216-92e1-53f5-b4d6-87d88a93a1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0584f1-0aae-50ac-b6e5-640ece58a243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a238c216-92e1-53f5-b4d6-87d88a93a1f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297577} :answer-field/id #uuid "bde7448d-6255-54c0-936b-fe929ae4a8c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9314e42-73f2-5134-b5e1-c3785c0ac3fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-338254" :question/problem "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+3y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=3.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot (-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6274c88-2ef0-57f1-ae3d-efd546ade707" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297581} {:answer/id #uuid "8e18c4c9-bac6-5c52-9e0e-e46c31185d7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297582} {:answer/id #uuid "a45bd06b-e2dd-5deb-9b51-29c6c987aec3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297583} {:answer/id #uuid "6e1fcc35-f541-567a-b932-e1f3c8e8c7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297584} {:answer/id #uuid "5a418329-a5a3-5cc4-b323-e78511469171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e1fcc35-f541-567a-b932-e1f3c8e8c7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297584} :answer-field/id #uuid "c66c4006-a6a8-572f-93af-4a6a32bb0e84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "39f6ec50-e251-5f95-8416-ba7803d7b734" :question/math-academy-id "q-65038" :question/problem "Given that $D={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=2{x}^{3}+4?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}={x}^{2},{f}_{1}=-x,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(2{x}^{3}+4) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})(2{x}^{3}+4) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2{x}^{3}+4)-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+4) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{2})-x\\cdot 6{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 12x-6{x}^{3} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}-6{x}^{3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e79691b-5ad7-599f-9391-83d158f8d740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297588} {:answer/id #uuid "72d14904-335d-5485-9acb-bd95742bc07b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297589} {:answer/id #uuid "ee19f2ab-3418-5312-bd3c-b419a7d16abf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297590} {:answer/id #uuid "34b84bfb-baaf-50dc-823f-874c9988d8a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12{e}^{-2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297591} {:answer/id #uuid "8391cc75-b6a9-5f4f-bd14-770febf23ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8391cc75-b6a9-5f4f-bd14-770febf23ed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297592} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff273fa0-2b0d-5acf-a637-db706a4de5f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "640d72a2-ebb8-5406-9cba-a5d7630ef9f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-65055" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y={e}^{-2x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients ${a}_{3}=1,{a}_{2}=4,{a}_{1}=4,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-2x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}){e}^{-2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{-2x})+4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-2x})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-2x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(-2{e}^{-2x})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{e}^{-2x})+4\\cdot (-2{e}^{-2x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{-2x})+4\\cdot 4{e}^{-2x}-8{e}^{-2x} \\\\  & =-8{e}^{-2x}+16{e}^{-2x}-8{e}^{-2x} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1ff5fef-dfc8-5f90-9e68-709ffa999b26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297595} {:answer/id #uuid "37c29747-2693-5054-ad6f-903b71a2720b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297596} {:answer/id #uuid "16335570-faa1-54a2-a02e-1201972d95b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297597} {:answer/id #uuid "5952ce3f-6d68-52c0-a877-1ef0389e6aa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297598} {:answer/id #uuid "96eb6d9c-b93b-5ffa-967d-6ffbd57dcc88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96eb6d9c-b93b-5ffa-967d-6ffbd57dcc88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297599} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed2b92a-d1ce-591e-a158-29fb029bd684" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1f384bed-894a-5dfa-9b9b-225075b79f42" :question/math-academy-id "q-79607" :question/problem "Given that $D=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\frac{1}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=-1,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Functions of X as Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7c7374b-430e-556c-baae-1268d123bdf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297602} {:answer/id #uuid "18a4d3bd-1165-53ef-868b-88d45dace9fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297603} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c5b620-6b8b-5844-b4dd-4679430b1239" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297604} {:answer/id #uuid "11c4833c-96aa-5bcc-afc1-f53a43cd3ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297605} {:answer/id #uuid "7b6cb180-fc97-577f-bb3c-3b21b07591b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11c4833c-96aa-5bcc-afc1-f53a43cd3ef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297605} :answer-field/id #uuid "dbb18c8f-ab80-5b73-a097-538a33eda7d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf6fe938-eeca-5659-860f-4454a76fa5a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-91035" :question/problem "Given that $D={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}={x}^{2},{f}_{1}=x,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x)+x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{x}+1)+x(\\frac{2}{x}+1) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})+x(\\frac{2}{x}+1) \\\\  & =-2+2+x \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297607 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ec3823db-6df8-502a-a050-b5aa169d2e9d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Differential Operators With Constant Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be93ea2-7f60-58d7-b17e-8968f5f00057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297609} {:answer/id #uuid "767f4861-3e1b-585f-897d-8c2cdb047926" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297610} {:answer/id #uuid "3a50cf21-6df8-591c-a557-db030465e7f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297611} {:answer/id #uuid "779efa50-a695-57f7-a2da-9fafde3faa7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297612} {:answer/id #uuid "96fe6fce-1c12-543a-9682-168f0ecfab99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3be93ea2-7f60-58d7-b17e-8968f5f00057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297609} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba3ed9f6-456d-5756-8dca-e46f64cf17c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4a50f529-7a80-5ccf-9921-0fe6086a3323" :question/math-academy-id "q-91043" :question/problem "Given that $D=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-3\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={a}_{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{a}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{a}_{1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{a}_{0}y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  ${a}_{3}=1,{a}_{2}=-3,{a}_{1}=4,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-3\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-3\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-3(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
